#lang racket/base

;; Keyward's updater trust root: the Ed25519 public key and key ID that the
;; future explicit-consent update UI (issue #15) verifies release feeds
;; against. Per docs/UPDATE-SECURITY.md, the trusted public key and exact
;; key ID are pinned into the shipped application build — never supplied by
;; the feed being verified.
;;
;; Until the remaining issue #15 rungs (platform handoffs, upgrade CI, the
;; Check for Updates UI) land, Keyward stays manual-update-only: nothing in
;; the application contacts a release server. The release feed is already
;; signed in CI with this key (scripts/make-update-manifest.sh), so the
;; signature chain exists before any consumer does.
;;
;; Rotation (docs/UPDATE-SECURITY.md): ship a build that trusts the next key
;; before signing releases exclusively with it. The private half lives only
;; in the release secret store (UPDATE_ED25519_PRIVATE_KEY_B64) and the
;; operator's synced key vault; it never enters the repository.

(require net/base64)

(provide update-public-key-b64
         update-key-id)

;; SubjectPublicKeyInfo DER, base64. Generated by
;; scripts/gen-update-keys.sh (Racket crypto, same library the verification
;; uses — proves the DER round-trips through rivet's own readers).
(define update-public-key-b64
  "MCowBQYDK2VwAyEA+h2Mg/lYsYhA6ny3ekbklBuK3d6JGWCeiIWS+NwzmHc=")

;; Rivet's signed-manifest key id; rotate together with the key above.
(define update-key-id "keyward-2026-11")
